Wait, why is it that I can't type the letter 'k' inside the search box? I am seeing that I can't do CTRL-k and then k - that doesn't work. It's beacause keyCombinationCanHappen boolean is set to be true whenever CTRL is pressed. So the moment I press k it starts to focus on the input element, which is what I wanted to happen on the FIRST time the k is pressed. I think I need to check whether I can access the "last key pressed".

Okay, I am back and I have solved it. I tried the array of keys pressed method but it was a bit janky, so I avoided it and relied on traditional event.key instead. Now I have introduced another variable - keyCombinationActivated - which is a boolean and it's set to true if CTRL-K is pressed. So the sequence of events is this: the user presses CTRL -> keyCombinationCanHappen is set to true -> they press k next -> keyCombinationActivated is true -> if keyCombinationActivated is true, we set everything back to false so that we can await future key combinations. This means that keyCombinationCanHappen is again false and that means that typing k in is now allowed and doesn't focus on the input now, as keyCombinationCanHappen is false and the condition is invalid.

